{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116408",
      "title": "Working with Nested Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 277,
      "videoOrder": 264,
      "sourceHash": "329ae21817a937b20cd641eca7615a937c16bbfbac2a9d580d79776d74c7cf05",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 2.94,
          "en": "Now, slowly but steadily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.94,
          "end": 6.12,
          "en": "this application is taking shape.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.12,
          "end": 8.61,
          "en": "But now as a next step, it would be nice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.61,
          "end": 12.93,
          "en": "to actually load the tasks of a user here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.93,
          "end": 15.376,
          "en": "And for that we could of course go to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.376,
          "end": 20.16,
          "en": "that user tasks component and not just load",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.16,
          "end": 21.75,
          "en": "and set the username here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.75,
          "end": 24.99,
          "en": "but also retrieve tasks for that user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24.99,
          "end": 28.503,
          "en": "and then output the tasks here instead of this to-do text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.34,
          "end": 30.48,
          "en": "We could do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.48,
          "end": 33.15,
          "en": "And depending on our application requirements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.15,
          "end": 36.071,
          "en": "that might be exactly what we wanna do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.071,
          "end": 40.29,
          "en": "Here, however, I actually want to work with nested routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.29,
          "end": 42.42,
          "en": "and one reason of course is that I want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.42,
          "end": 45.09,
          "en": "to show you the concept of nested routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.09,
          "end": 48.57,
          "en": "because it's an important one in Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.57,
          "end": 49.8,
          "en": "But another reason is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.8,
          "end": 54.51,
          "en": "that we actually have two different routes that we can load",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 54.51,
          "end": 55.647,
          "en": "for every user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.647,
          "end": 60.61,
          "en": "because we might want to show the tasks here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 60.61,
          "end": 64.47,
          "en": "but we also might want to allow the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.47,
          "end": 66.27,
          "en": "to add a new task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 66.27,
          "end": 68.73,
          "en": "So we might wanna show a form here that allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 68.73,
          "end": 70.383,
          "en": "to add a new task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.34,
          "end": 75.87,
          "en": "And therefore we should go back to the app.routes.ts file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.87,
          "end": 79.35,
          "en": "and register two new routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.35,
          "end": 83.88,
          "en": "But the goal now actually is to register these routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.88,
          "end": 88.88,
          "en": "as child routes for this user's user id route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 89.239,
          "end": 94.239,
          "en": "Because child routes are a special Angular routing feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 98.49000000000001,
          "en": "that allows us to work with nested router outlets.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 98.49000000000001,
          "end": 100.14,
          "en": "And it will essentially allow us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 100.14,
          "end": 104.49000000000001,
          "en": "to load a component into another component that was loaded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.49000000000001,
          "end": 106.02000000000001,
          "en": "because of another route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 106.02000000000001,
          "end": 108.663,
          "en": "And you'll see how it works in just a second.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.97999999999999,
          "end": 113.7,
          "en": "You set up child routes by adding the children property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.7,
          "end": 115.92,
          "en": "to the route to which you want to add it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.92,
          "end": 117.836,
          "en": "So in my case to this route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.836,
          "end": 121.71,
          "en": "And then this takes another array of routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 121.71,
          "end": 124.11,
          "en": "where the route objects look exactly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.11,
          "end": 127.143,
          "en": "as they do in the main array of routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 131.13,
          "en": "So every route here has a path and a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.13,
          "end": 133.56,
          "en": "and potentially some other configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.56,
          "end": 136.215,
          "en": "which we will explore later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.215,
          "end": 140.034,
          "en": "Though what's important to note about this path here is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.034,
          "end": 145.034,
          "en": "that it will automatically be concatenated to this path.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.2,
          "end": 148.53,
          "en": "So these child routes will automatically take the parent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.53,
          "end": 151.653,
          "en": "route path and append their own paths.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 152.871,
          "end": 156.15,
          "en": "So for example, here we could add tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 156.15,
          "end": 159.43099999999998,
          "en": "and this would lead to this kind of route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 159.43099999999998,
          "end": 164.43099999999998,
          "en": "where we have our domain /users/some user ID/tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 165.27,
          "end": 168.663,
          "en": "because it's configured as a child route to this route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 170.82,
          "end": 174.993,
          "en": "Then here, I might want to show the tasks component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.55,
          "end": 179.7,
          "en": "Now if I would save that like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.7,
          "end": 182.55,
          "en": "if you add /tasks here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.55,
          "end": 186.6,
          "en": "after /users/ slash some user id,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 186.6,
          "end": 189.72,
          "en": "you will not get the desired result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.72,
          "end": 194.01,
          "en": "The tasks component is not showing up anywhere on the screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 194.01,
          "end": 198.09,
          "en": "because we're currently not telling Angular where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 198.09,
          "end": 201.273,
          "en": "to render this route here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 202.53,
          "end": 206.13,
          "en": "You might say that we have a router outlet here in the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 206.13,
          "end": 209.34,
          "en": "component, but that's for our main routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 209.34,
          "end": 213.63,
          "en": "Child routes like this one here need a separate router",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 213.63,
          "end": 217.233,
          "en": "outlet in the component of which they are a child of.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 218.13,
          "end": 220.26,
          "en": "So we need to add a router outlet in",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 220.26,
          "end": 224.43,
          "en": "that user tasks component so that the child components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 224.43,
          "end": 227.373,
          "en": "of this route here can be loaded there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 228.51,
          "end": 232.68,
          "en": "So we need to go to the user tasks component HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 232.68,
          "end": 235.903,
          "en": "And there it's this placeholder paragraph",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 235.903,
          "end": 239.133,
          "en": "that should be replaced with a router outlet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 240.48,
          "end": 243.48,
          "en": "And for that to be available here, we need to go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 243.48,
          "end": 246.75,
          "en": "to the user tasks component TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 246.75,
          "end": 249.546,
          "en": "and there add this imports array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 249.546,
          "end": 252.96,
          "en": "and add the router outlet here, which",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 252.96,
          "end": 256.113,
          "en": "of course also must be imported from Angular router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 258,
          "end": 260.85,
          "en": "And with that, if you save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 260.85,
          "end": 265.85,
          "en": "if you visit /users/U2/tasks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 266.19,
          "end": 270.202,
          "en": "you will see this task component being out put here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 270.202,
          "end": 273.75,
          "en": "So that's a step in the right direction.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 273.75,
          "end": 277.23,
          "en": "As a next step, I also want to register a route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 277.23,
          "end": 279.54,
          "en": "for adding new tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 279.54,
          "end": 281.55,
          "en": "before we then of course want to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 281.55,
          "end": 284.25,
          "en": "that we load the user specific tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 284.25,
          "end": 287.578,
          "en": "and that we make sure that users can also add new tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 287.578,
          "end": 290.90999999999997,
          "en": "through that new task component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 290.90999999999997,
          "end": 294.723,
          "en": "But let's start by adding another route for that new task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 295.86,
          "end": 298.953,
          "en": "And here the goal is to have a path of tasks/new.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 301.23,
          "end": 303.334,
          "en": "And then the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 303.334,
          "end": 306.333,
          "en": "that should be loaded is the new task component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 307.2,
          "end": 309.21,
          "en": "And that should be all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 309.21,
          "end": 311.22,
          "en": "If you save that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 311.22,
          "end": 316.22,
          "en": "and you enter /users/ some valid user ID/tasks/new,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 320.13,
          "end": 322.413,
          "en": "this form here shows up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 322.413,
          "end": 326.4,
          "en": "and that shows you how nested routes work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 326.4,
          "end": 328.683,
          "en": "Now let's make them a bit more useful.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
